>280 HP at level 17

  With the Orb of Fate's half-physical-damage attribute that's
the equivalent of 560 hit points.


  Plenty of people have ascended with a lot fewer equivalent 
hit points.  As many or more have ascended at level 17 or lower.

  The main reason I see for leveling up past level 17 is 
hit/mana points, neither of which you really need more of.

  After that, the extra skill slots are nice for #enhancing spell
skills.  Again, probably not a concern for your Valk.

  So I don't think you have any pressing need to waste 
time/resources level ling up your character.  (Note I normally
keep "pseudo-levelling up" even after reaching level 30 for
the mana points.  But that's for wizards.  A wizard is worth
the massive extra effort for that, imho.  But not a valk.)


  The most important piece of an ascension kit (after bell,
book, candelabrum, and 7 candles) is an ascension state of
mind.  (Which you seem to be moving toward.)

  A quick summary of the ascension state of mind:

     1. Don't die.  (This is a bad sign even with an AoLS)
     2. Once you've done the invocation:

	  - Don't fight if you can RUN!


  Further endgame hints(very spoily), including a way to 
double your traveling speed on Astral, Fire, and Earth planes,
are here:


<http://groups.google.co.uk/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/msg/447d6aaa0922f424>

<http://groups.google.co.uk/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/msg/f7a4ba3e0e14dd77>


  There are other posts in that thread worth reading.



  If a chance to easily gain a level falls into your lap, take 
it.  Otherwise, don't bother.

  Should you choose to ignore my splendid ;^D advice and spend 
extra effort to level up, what follows are my comments on
how to do that.
  

>
>ANYHOW.....my question is simple.....How do I gain the needed levels to
>ascend?? I am getting close to the end (sort of), but given the rate of
>xp gain so far, I don't see myself gaining more than 2 or 3 more levels
>through normal combat.

  You may get one more level through normal combat, possibly two.
The experience points requirements for level gain double with 
each level gained.  (Close enough, anyway.)


>
>
>I know wraith corpses give you a level when eaten, but I have no idea
>how to preserve them long enough to eat. Tinning doesn't work, and they
>fade quickly.

   Just eat them when you find them, UNLESS you are SATIATED.

Instadeath by choking on a nutritionless wraith corpse is a nasty
experience.  (If you're wearing an amulet of magical breathing
you can risk eating the corpse regardless of satiated status.)

>
>
>Potions of gain level are nice, but very rare for me.

  They can be alchemized, but I don't recommend it.

